<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">International Committee of the Red Cross</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1863">1863</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as ICRC</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The International Committee of the Red Cross is a humanitarian organisation founded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geneva">Geneva</a> in 1863 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-dunant">Henry Dunant</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guillaume-henri-dufour">Guillaume-Henri Dufour</a> and three other citizens. It inspired the Geneva Conventions and works to protect and assist victims of war, visiting prisoners of war, tracing missing persons and promoting humanitarian law. It received the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nobel-peace-prize">Nobel Peace Prize</a> in 1917, 1944 and 1963.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/international-committee-of-the-red-cross.jpg" alt="International Committee of the Red Cross" width="320" height="376" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: International Committee of the Red Cross · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emblem_of_the_ICRC.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
